chapter.v:
Remove far 


from me, 


falsehood and lying; give me neither poverty nor riches; feed me with the food that is needful for me,

a slave 


when he, 


becomes king, and a fool when he is filled with food;

the ants 


are a, 


people not strong, yet they provide their food in the summer;

the rock 


badgers are, 


a people not mighty, yet they make their homes in the cliffs;

the locusts 


have no, 


king, yet all of them march in rank;

the lion, 


which is, 


mightiest among beasts and does not turn back before any;
